WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:04.670 --> 00:06.330
Rei's after a junior at my school.

3
00:06.330 --> 00:07.630
Mii, just break up with Rei.

4
00:07.630 --> 00:08.900
I'm going to break up with him.

5
00:08.900 --> 00:09.970
And you cheated on me.

6
00:09.970 --> 00:11.370
How could you do this?

7
00:12.770 --> 00:14.070
We don't need to really kiss.

8
00:14.070 --> 00:15.970
I don't think it'll look convincing.

9
00:15.970 --> 00:17.430
Because in a stage play,

10
00:17.430 --> 00:19.200
the audience sees from every angle.

11
00:19.200 --> 00:20.700
I agree with Kim.

12
00:20.700 --> 00:22.100
And me, as the audience?

13
00:22.100 --> 00:23.100
I'm totally fine with it.

14
00:23.100 --> 00:23.900
Kiss for real.

15
00:23.900 --> 00:24.900
Din!

16
00:26.600 --> 00:28.130
I worried you'd get the wrong idea.

17
00:28.130 --> 00:29.430
Will you change on me, Aof?

18
00:29.430 --> 00:31.100
Are you only being nice to me for now?

19
00:31.100 --> 00:33.130
You don't have to believe my words, Chemi.

20
00:33.130 --> 00:34.470
Just watch what I do.

21
00:34.470 --> 00:36.130
I'll be watching closely.

22
00:36.130 --> 00:39.530
If we talk in here, it's not cheating, right?

23
00:39.530 --> 00:41.470
I know you take good care of yourself, Time,

24
00:41.470 --> 00:43.000
but let me care for you better.

25
00:43.000 --> 00:44.370
You said you'd take care of me.

26
00:44.370 --> 00:46.170
Bathe me, then. / Mm.

27
00:46.170 --> 00:47.700
Mind your eyes.

28
00:47.700 --> 00:49.370
Then don't move so much.

29
00:49.370 --> 00:52.500
You got ICL's offer. What are you waiting for?

30
00:52.500 --> 00:54.470
Why didn't you ever think to tell me?

31
00:54.470 --> 00:55.870
I don't want to see you anymore.

32
00:55.870 --> 00:56.700
Go wherever.

33
00:57.400 --> 00:59.070
You're so damn selfish.

34
01:01.500 --> 01:03.700
I don't know what to do anymore.

35
01:04.099 --> 01:06.200
This is my whole life.

36
01:06.200 --> 01:07.430
You're not alone, Mii.

37
01:07.430 --> 01:08.930
You still have me.

38
01:32.000 --> 01:33.270
And that asshole Rei?

39
01:33.270 --> 01:34.930
Is he taking responsibility?

40
01:37.370 --> 01:38.729
He's not answering.

41
01:41.400 --> 01:43.700
I don't know how to tell my parents.

42
01:44.000 --> 01:45.000
It's okay, Mii.

43
01:46.000 --> 01:47.330
I'll go with you.

44
01:47.600 --> 01:49.030
I'm not leaving you alone in this.

45
01:49.570 --> 01:51.170
Don't be scared, Mii.

46
02:07.270 --> 02:09.330
Rei, you fucker. The baby. What are you gonna do?

47
02:09.330 --> 02:11.470
Huh? That's your kid, asshole.

48
02:12.430 --> 02:15.830
This is between me and Mii. Stay the fuck out of it.

49
02:15.830 --> 02:17.800
Hey, stop! / Rei, you asshole!

50
02:17.800 --> 02:19.370
I said stop.

51
02:20.630 --> 02:21.470
Stop it!

52
02:23.200 --> 02:26.200
Are you taking responsibility? Answer me!

53
02:26.200 --> 02:27.600
You've had time to think.

54
02:28.070 --> 02:29.970
Don't just stand there, you coward.

55
02:29.970 --> 02:30.870
Shut up, asshole.

56
02:30.870 --> 02:31.800
You shut up.

57
02:32.130 --> 02:35.000
Did you even think? Do you ever use your brain?

58
02:35.000 --> 02:36.970
Responsible for what? Spit it out.

59
02:37.200 --> 02:38.970
Then, Mii, why don't you tell me

60
02:38.970 --> 02:40.800
what you want me to do

61
02:40.800 --> 02:42.100
to make you happy?

62
02:43.900 --> 02:45.000
Go on, tell me.

63
02:45.000 --> 02:46.000
Don't touch my friend.

64
02:46.000 --> 02:47.000
Butt out.

65
02:47.000 --> 02:47.930
You butt out.

66
02:49.430 --> 02:51.500
Make me happy?

67
02:51.500 --> 02:53.800
Fine. I'll tell you.

68
02:54.600 --> 02:56.329
Get out of my life.

69
02:59.130 --> 03:00.400
And stay away from me.

70
03:00.800 --> 03:01.630
Go!

71
03:02.530 --> 03:04.670
Didn't you hear my friend? Go!

72
03:05.000 --> 03:07.170
You're not me. You don't get it.

73
03:07.170 --> 03:08.430
Why don't you try being me?

74
03:08.430 --> 03:10.930
Even if I were you, I'd never leave Mii alone.

75
03:11.270 --> 03:13.030
That baby is yours.

76
03:13.030 --> 03:14.570
You won't take responsibility?

77
03:17.500 --> 03:20.230
Just go. / Go!

78
03:20.230 --> 03:22.030
And don't you ever come back.

79
03:22.030 --> 03:23.700
My friend loves me more than you do.

80
03:23.700 --> 03:27.100
Go. Get out.

81
03:27.100 --> 03:29.200
Fine, I'm going. Asshole.

82
03:41.070 --> 03:43.770
It's okay, Mii. You still have me.

83
03:44.470 --> 03:46.700
He's just one shitty guy.

84
03:47.170 --> 03:48.670
You're not alone, Mii.

85
03:49.000 --> 03:50.530
Don't be scared.

86
03:50.970 --> 03:52.300
You've got me.

87
03:57.900 --> 03:59.300
Don't be scared, Mii.

88
07:09.870 --> 07:12.130
You okay?

89
07:32.400 --> 07:34.630
It's Aof, isn't it?

90
07:44.070 --> 07:47.170
Bro, talk some sense into me.

91
07:48.470 --> 07:50.930
I don't want to get hurt anymore.

92
08:10.670 --> 08:12.730
You've been so brave.

93
08:17.070 --> 08:20.400
Putting your whole heart into loving someone

94
08:22.230 --> 08:24.400
is a really good thing.

95
08:28.670 --> 08:30.270
It only just happened.

96
08:34.299 --> 08:35.830
It's okay to be sad.

97
08:38.600 --> 08:40.700
Just don't stay sad for too long.

98
08:41.270 --> 08:42.700
I worry about you.

99
08:53.200 --> 08:55.970
We'll always have each other, Chemi.

100
08:58.870 --> 09:00.770
Don't cry.

101
09:03.000 --> 09:04.630
I love you.

102
09:05.530 --> 09:07.400
I love you too, Bro.

103
09:48.070 --> 09:50.800
You sure you don't want me to come up with you?

104
09:57.270 --> 09:58.030
Mm-hm.

105
09:59.630 --> 10:01.430
Thanks, Aof.

106
10:02.430 --> 10:05.600
If anything comes up, you can always call me.

107
10:20.600 --> 10:23.330
I'm always on your side, Mii.

108
10:43.770 --> 10:45.130
Memii?

109
10:46.170 --> 10:49.570
What's wrong, sweetie? Why are you crying?

110
10:49.570 --> 10:51.770
Tell me what happened.

111
10:53.030 --> 10:55.000
Dad, Mom...

112
10:56.130 --> 10:58.630
I'm sorry.

113
11:06.200 --> 11:08.230
I'm pregnant.

114
11:20.400 --> 11:23.000
Are you going to hate me, Mom?

115
11:23.000 --> 11:25.800
No, no. Don't say that, sweetheart.

116
11:25.800 --> 11:28.970
It's okay, honey. Don't cry.

117
11:29.600 --> 11:32.170
We'll figure this out together.

118
11:57.930 --> 12:01.030
I can't do a damn thing.

119
12:01.600 --> 12:04.170
Mii asked how I'd take care of her,

120
12:04.530 --> 12:07.030
and I couldn't even answer.

121
12:12.800 --> 12:16.900
So what are you going to do now?

122
12:19.700 --> 12:21.500
I don't know.

123
12:23.430 --> 12:25.230
Someone like me

124
12:25.800 --> 12:27.670
is better off alone.

125
12:28.200 --> 12:31.230
I don't want to cause trouble for anyone anymore.

126
12:34.100 --> 12:35.830
It's okay, man.

127
12:35.830 --> 12:37.770
You've got us.

128
13:09.300 --> 13:12.000
Chemi, I'm sorry.

129
13:12.370 --> 13:13.630
I'm outside your house.

130
13:14.030 --> 13:15.700
Can you come out for a bit?

131
13:15.900 --> 13:17.330
I want to explain.

132
13:17.330 --> 13:19.100
Why are you here?

133
13:19.100 --> 13:20.630
I'm going to bed.

134
13:42.400 --> 13:43.800
I'm not tired.

135
13:43.800 --> 13:45.900
Because I'm not even trying.

136
13:53.730 --> 13:56.430
I told you, this time I'll do my best.

137
13:56.430 --> 14:01.400
♪ Like every day, things keep getting harder ♪

138
14:01.400 --> 14:06.830
♪ Like every moment, nothing is ever clear ♪

139
14:06.830 --> 14:12.100
♪ It's like the love we had is too hard to understand ♪

140
14:12.100 --> 14:17.630
♪ It's like as time goes on, in my heart ♪

141
14:17.630 --> 14:22.600
♪ Something has begun, and it's getting complicated ♪

142
14:22.600 --> 14:28.600
♪ There's more to it than that ♪

143
14:28.600 --> 14:36.900
♪ I can't find the answer ♪

144
14:38.830 --> 14:44.070
♪ If I'd known this was all the road we had ♪

145
14:44.070 --> 14:49.470
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

146
14:49.470 --> 14:55.600
♪ But in the end the story stops right here ♪

147
14:55.600 --> 15:00.430
♪ We'll never get to love each other again ♪

148
15:00.430 --> 15:05.530
♪ If only I'd told you straight that day ♪

149
15:05.530 --> 15:11.130
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

150
15:11.130 --> 15:16.930
♪ But in the end the story stops right here ♪

151
15:16.930 --> 15:25.600
♪ You and I were never meant to be ♪

152
15:40.870 --> 15:42.570
And I'm shooting you with it right now.

153
15:42.570 --> 15:43.670
Be my model.

154
15:44.400 --> 15:45.400
No way.

155
15:45.400 --> 15:46.700
I hate photos of me.

156
15:48.170 --> 15:49.800
But I like taking pictures of you.

157
15:56.470 --> 15:59.900
Are you sure about this? I'm really not confident.

158
16:00.530 --> 16:09.700
♪ I can't find the answer ♪

159
16:10.730 --> 16:15.670
♪ If I'd known this was all the road we had ♪

160
16:15.670 --> 16:21.730
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

161
16:23.830 --> 16:26.330
When you like someone,

162
16:26.330 --> 16:30.230
you just put yourself close to them.

163
16:31.430 --> 16:33.100
Take a picture with me.

164
16:33.500 --> 16:35.300
...is already the best there is.

165
16:38.330 --> 16:42.930
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

166
16:42.930 --> 16:49.200
♪ But in the end the story stops right here ♪

167
16:49.200 --> 16:55.970
♪ You and I were never meant to be ♪

168
17:05.800 --> 17:07.400
You've liked me since M.2?

169
17:07.400 --> 17:08.470
How did you stand it?

170
17:09.700 --> 17:11.470
Because I like you so damn much, I guess.

171
17:11.869 --> 17:13.599
But for me,

172
17:14.700 --> 17:17.030
I never saw you as just a friend to begin with.

173
17:18.170 --> 17:19.130
If I don't lie to you,

174
17:19.130 --> 17:21.130
you'll leave me, right? / I don't want to see you.

175
17:21.130 --> 17:21.930
Go wherever.

176
17:21.930 --> 17:23.599
You're so damn selfish.

177
17:32.330 --> 17:34.730
I'm sorry, Fuen.

178
17:36.000 --> 17:38.030
I never wanted it to be like this.

179
17:38.930 --> 17:41.500
I don't want to lose you.

180
17:41.500 --> 17:45.830
♪ We'll never get to love each other again ♪

181
17:45.830 --> 17:51.630
♪ If only I'd told you straight that day ♪

182
17:51.630 --> 17:56.400
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

183
17:56.400 --> 18:02.870
♪ And in the end the story stops right here ♪

184
18:02.870 --> 18:11.370
♪ You and I were never meant to be ♪

185
18:23.730 --> 18:30.430
♪ You and I... ♪

186
18:52.230 --> 18:57.170
"3 Weeks Later"

187
19:19.000 --> 19:21.770
Oh, Fuen. What are you up to, honey?

188
19:22.230 --> 19:23.470
Washing the car, Mom.

189
19:23.470 --> 19:24.570
What does it look like?

190
19:24.570 --> 19:28.830
Physics usually comes over to wash it for you. Where is he today?

191
19:30.330 --> 19:32.670
Why would I ask him? I can do it myself.

192
19:32.670 --> 19:34.430
Is something going on?

193
19:35.400 --> 19:38.200
If you don't stop asking, I'm washing you too.

194
19:38.200 --> 19:41.900
Fine, suit yourself. Look how clumsy you are. Whatever you say.

195
20:59.030 --> 21:05.330
"You really don't want to see me anymore, Fuen?"

196
21:20.000 --> 21:23.870
"Fuen, I'm sorry. I miss you."

197
22:36.100 --> 22:40.930
"Done with tutoring."

198
22:45.800 --> 22:49.800
If we talk in here, it's not cheating, right?

199
22:49.800 --> 22:52.870
Because we're talking through pictures.

200
23:09.670 --> 23:14.730
"Done with tutoring."

201
23:58.170 --> 24:01.900
Oh, Din. How long have you been here?

202
24:01.900 --> 24:04.930
Why didn't you have someone let you in?

203
24:04.930 --> 24:07.870
Or is something up?

204
24:08.300 --> 24:12.530
Well, I wanted to ask you to go to school with me.

205
24:15.330 --> 24:16.400
Perfect timing.

206
24:16.670 --> 24:18.470
I'm in a rush to get to a meeting.

207
24:19.130 --> 24:21.400
Star, you go with Din, then.

208
24:21.730 --> 24:22.930
Okay.

209
24:24.400 --> 24:27.600
Go on, get out. You'll be late for school.

210
24:27.600 --> 24:29.500
Yes, Dad.

211
24:32.200 --> 24:36.300
Hey, it's the second term. Study hard, you two.

212
24:37.200 --> 24:38.900
Samai, let's go.

213
24:38.900 --> 24:40.630
Let the kids do their flirting.

214
24:41.330 --> 24:42.700
Goodbye.

215
24:49.200 --> 24:51.900
So, we...

216
25:15.600 --> 25:17.130
Come with me.

217
25:52.300 --> 25:54.070
First time?

218
25:55.770 --> 25:57.070
Yeah.

219
25:57.070 --> 25:59.670
Ride the BTS with me more and you'll get the hang of it.

220
26:00.700 --> 26:03.500
So you're going to take me every day?

221
26:03.500 --> 26:07.230
If you don't mind the hassle, I'd like to.

222
26:07.230 --> 26:10.670
Then next time you come, wait inside the house.

223
26:10.670 --> 26:12.600
Don't stand out in the sun.

224
27:05.900 --> 27:06.900
Honey.

225
27:07.300 --> 27:09.570
You still haven't made up with Physics?

226
27:12.800 --> 27:14.670
How do you know?

227
27:15.930 --> 27:21.570
I'm your mother. Come on, tell me.

228
27:28.070 --> 27:30.100
Physics is going to study abroad.

229
27:30.700 --> 27:32.800
But he never told me.

230
27:32.800 --> 27:36.300
And then he has the nerve to say it all depends on my answer.

231
27:36.530 --> 27:38.130
Think about it, Mom.

232
27:38.130 --> 27:40.370
Say I don't agree to be his boyfriend.

233
27:40.370 --> 27:42.070
Then he'll just leave me.

234
27:42.770 --> 27:45.470
How am I supposed to not be hurt?

235
27:45.470 --> 27:46.970
I'm hurt.

236
27:50.600 --> 27:54.400
Honey, are you sure you're not imagining things?

237
27:55.930 --> 27:59.400
Did Physics actually say that if you won't be his boyfriend,

238
27:59.400 --> 28:01.500
he'll leave you?

239
28:02.470 --> 28:03.500
Well...

240
28:06.300 --> 28:09.530
See? You're imagining it.

241
28:11.830 --> 28:14.530
The university over there already accepted him.

242
28:15.000 --> 28:18.330
Whatever I answer, he's going anyway.

243
28:18.330 --> 28:21.230
So are you mad that Physics didn't tell you,

244
28:21.230 --> 28:23.470
or that you'll be apart?

245
28:28.230 --> 28:32.470
I want to be with him. Wherever we study,

246
28:33.200 --> 28:37.230
whatever faculty, I wouldn't mind.

247
28:37.800 --> 28:41.030
I just never thought we'd suddenly be so far apart.

248
28:41.900 --> 28:44.500
But have you thought about it from Physics's side?

249
28:44.500 --> 28:47.900
About why he wants an answer from you?

250
28:50.200 --> 28:55.770
That's not right, Mom. This is his future.

251
28:56.430 --> 28:59.200
What if he doesn't want to go because of me?

252
29:01.270 --> 29:03.400
I don't want to hold him back.

253
29:08.570 --> 29:11.800
Thanks for breakfast today, Mom.

254
29:11.800 --> 29:14.030
But you stay here at the shop today.

255
29:14.030 --> 29:16.370
I'll take the BTS myself.

256
29:17.300 --> 29:18.400
Bye, Mom.

257
29:27.070 --> 29:32.800
This second term, I want all Thapfah students to work hard and stay disciplined.

258
29:32.800 --> 29:36.730
You all did very well last term.

259
30:07.730 --> 30:10.270
Physics, let's talk.

260
30:21.800 --> 30:23.430
I'm sorry.

261
30:28.600 --> 30:30.930
I know I shouldn't have lost my temper.

262
30:32.830 --> 30:35.170
At the very least, I should've heard you out.

263
30:38.100 --> 30:40.430
Because you always have your reasons.

264
30:48.000 --> 30:50.200
I get that you're mad at me.

265
30:54.030 --> 30:57.300
But when you said you didn't want to see my face,

266
31:01.100 --> 31:03.200
I was lost.

267
31:06.430 --> 31:11.330
I'm sorry, but I want you to think about your future.

268
31:21.400 --> 31:23.270
You should go, Physics.

269
31:32.530 --> 31:34.300
Then can you tell me

270
31:35.170 --> 31:37.500
how you feel about me?

271
31:50.400 --> 31:51.530
It hurts

272
31:54.000 --> 31:59.300
that I can't even imagine who I'd be without you.

273
32:03.800 --> 32:09.300
Even in university, I want to be at the same school as you.

274
32:13.200 --> 32:15.530
Even though that's not possible anymore,

275
32:16.830 --> 32:18.430
I'll hang in there.

276
32:23.670 --> 32:25.100
So...

277
32:28.100 --> 32:30.300
Summer break, long holidays...

278
32:31.900 --> 32:36.770
come back to me. Because...

279
32:41.170 --> 32:44.030
I like you, Physics.

280
33:15.230 --> 33:18.200
Who said I'm going alone?

281
33:19.100 --> 33:20.700
Huh?

282
33:24.800 --> 33:26.330
You...

283
33:28.570 --> 33:30.470
Come study in England with me.

284
33:31.900 --> 33:33.600
How is that even possible?

285
33:33.600 --> 33:35.600
Have you seen my grades?

286
33:36.200 --> 33:37.470
That's fine.

287
33:37.470 --> 33:38.870
I'll help you.

288
33:39.670 --> 33:41.270
Just come with me.

289
33:43.270 --> 33:45.530
Didn't you already take the exams?

290
33:46.030 --> 33:50.270
A-Level and IELTS still have a second round.

291
33:51.130 --> 33:53.330
Pass this round, and you'll still make it in time.

292
33:56.130 --> 33:58.170
You've got it all planned out, huh?

293
34:04.370 --> 34:08.800
Well, every plan in my life...

294
34:10.370 --> 34:12.800
has always had you in it.

295
34:36.330 --> 34:37.600
It's identical.

296
34:37.600 --> 34:39.300
Identical how?

297
35:37.230 --> 35:38.500
Want breakfast?

298
35:46.500 --> 35:47.770
What?

299
35:56.970 --> 35:58.670
What's up?

300
36:08.630 --> 36:10.470
I'm sorry, Physics,

301
36:10.470 --> 36:12.170
for being all talk.

302
36:12.630 --> 36:14.200
Today I finally understand...

303
36:14.200 --> 36:16.430
why you wanted me to stay away from your brother.

304
36:17.330 --> 36:20.170
I'm the one who fucked up.

305
36:20.830 --> 36:23.330
But I love your brother like crazy.

306
36:23.330 --> 36:24.770
Love my brother like crazy?

307
36:25.870 --> 36:27.500
What fucking love?! / Hey, hey!

308
36:27.500 --> 36:30.670
Huh? My brother is fucking heartbroken too.

309
36:32.200 --> 36:35.970
Do you know how hard you made my brother cry?

310
36:38.570 --> 36:40.470
Chemi cried?

311
36:41.270 --> 36:44.330
But Mii was in real trouble that day. I couldn't leave her.

312
36:44.330 --> 36:46.370
How many more times do I cut you slack?

313
36:47.870 --> 36:49.870
I warned you last time.

314
36:51.000 --> 36:52.930
What did you tell me?

315
36:52.930 --> 36:55.400
You told me this would never happen again.

316
36:56.230 --> 36:57.830
So why'd you do it again?

317
37:00.900 --> 37:02.600
This is my last warning.

318
37:03.600 --> 37:05.070
Stay away from my brother.

319
37:05.500 --> 37:06.770
Physics, but...

320
37:06.770 --> 37:08.570
Hey! Physics!

321
37:11.000 --> 37:12.970
Fuen, let go of me.

322
37:14.170 --> 37:16.330
Can't you give me one more chance?

323
37:16.700 --> 37:19.400
Another chance, and then what? What will you say?

324
37:19.400 --> 37:21.300
That you love my brother?

325
37:21.300 --> 37:23.800
If you really loved him, you'd have changed by now.

326
37:24.830 --> 37:29.130
Do you even realize? You say one thing and do another.

327
37:29.870 --> 37:32.200
You want me to play the fool and trust you?

328
37:34.170 --> 37:35.930
You should wise up already.

329
37:36.470 --> 37:37.870
And let my brother go.

330
37:37.870 --> 37:40.470
That's the one thing I just can't do.

331
37:40.770 --> 37:41.830
That's enough, Physics.

332
37:41.830 --> 37:44.600
You can hit me as many times as you want.

333
37:44.600 --> 37:47.170
But can't you give me a chance?

334
37:51.530 --> 37:53.300
A chance?

335
37:55.270 --> 37:57.930
A chance, after seeing my brother cry like that?

336
38:02.800 --> 38:04.730
As your friend, I'm sorry,

337
38:08.000 --> 38:09.900
but you're all talk.

338
38:13.030 --> 38:14.530
No chance.

339
38:15.930 --> 38:16.930
Physics!

340
38:17.670 --> 38:18.670
Physics!

341
38:18.670 --> 38:20.600
Aof, that's enough for today.

342
38:26.230 --> 38:28.130
Give him some time.

343
38:43.100 --> 38:45.530
You're always full of surprises.

344
38:47.230 --> 38:50.500
It's a shame we won't see it through together.

345
38:51.600 --> 38:57.900
But I understand. It's good you know early what you want to do.

346
38:59.330 --> 39:00.500
Thank you, Coach.

347
39:02.200 --> 39:03.800
I'm off to practice.

348
39:07.070 --> 39:08.170
Chemi.

349
39:17.230 --> 39:20.370
I'm sorry, Chemi, for not telling you what I was doing first.

350
39:20.900 --> 39:24.000
But I really didn't mean to leave you.

351
39:26.600 --> 39:33.230
Do you know your words and your actions don't match?

352
39:34.330 --> 39:37.370
You say you didn't mean to leave me,

353
39:38.030 --> 39:39.770
but you did.

354
39:40.430 --> 39:43.700
You even know what kind of person you are,

355
39:45.030 --> 39:48.130
and you still want me to trust you.

356
39:49.870 --> 39:55.600
Did you think I'd just wait around for you like an idiot?

357
39:55.600 --> 39:58.030
That's not it, Chemi. I never thought that. But...

358
39:58.400 --> 40:00.930
My friend was in trouble. I couldn't leave my friend.

359
40:00.930 --> 40:03.030
Once I'd helped her, I rushed right to you.

360
40:03.030 --> 40:03.830
But, Chemi...

361
40:03.830 --> 40:05.130
You couldn't leave your friend.

362
40:06.700 --> 40:08.630
But you could leave me.

363
40:18.200 --> 40:20.500
I'm asking seriously.

364
40:22.500 --> 40:28.530
Did you ever care, or ever think about me at all?

365
40:30.930 --> 40:33.200
That's not it, Chemi. I think of you all the time.

366
40:33.200 --> 40:34.500
Just stop, Aof.

367
40:37.500 --> 40:39.400
I don't want to hear it anymore.

368
40:42.900 --> 40:45.330
I can't trust you anymore.

369
40:46.500 --> 40:47.970
I've had enough

370
40:48.500 --> 40:50.630
of everything about you.

371
40:52.270 --> 40:54.970
Did I say something wrong again, Chemi?

372
40:57.700 --> 41:02.900
No. You didn't say anything wrong.

373
41:05.330 --> 41:07.470
It's my fault for expecting anything.

374
41:09.830 --> 41:10.830
And from now on,

375
41:10.830 --> 41:13.030
you don't need to try anymore.

376
41:14.070 --> 41:15.230
I don't want it anymore.

377
41:15.230 --> 41:16.370
Chemi.

378
41:18.300 --> 41:19.430
Chemi!

379
41:27.000 --> 41:28.500
Damn it!

380
41:47.130 --> 41:49.430
Man, why is he acting like this?

381
41:49.430 --> 41:52.170
If there were a ball right here, I'd kick it straight in his face.

382
41:52.900 --> 41:54.700
And I'd jump up and bite his ear.

383
41:54.700 --> 41:56.730
Still not satisfied, buddy?

384
41:56.730 --> 41:58.200
I'd kick his legs too.

385
41:58.200 --> 41:59.670
Enough.

386
42:06.130 --> 42:08.070
Don't go quiet on us, man.

387
42:08.070 --> 42:11.170
At least vent to me. I want to hear it.

388
42:17.130 --> 42:20.830
I'm fine with you leaving the club, but don't shut us out like this.

389
42:21.530 --> 42:23.370
I'm not okay.

390
42:25.000 --> 42:26.500
I just need some time.

391
42:27.270 --> 42:32.170
I'll be okay. Thanks.

392
43:03.130 --> 43:08.630
Twin... Twinkle... Twinkle?

393
43:13.500 --> 43:17.230
It can't be Twinkle Little Star, can it?

394
43:48.100 --> 43:49.730
What are you doing, Din?

395
43:50.300 --> 43:51.400
Whoa!

396
43:55.830 --> 43:59.430
Guess all you want, you'll never get it.

397
44:00.530 --> 44:03.730
I just wanted to try guessing.

398
44:08.600 --> 44:11.900
You have a meeting first today, right?

399
44:13.530 --> 44:17.000
Yeah. Shouldn't take long. Why?

400
44:17.600 --> 44:18.900
No reason.

401
44:19.370 --> 44:22.630
Then come back quickly after your meeting.

402
44:23.430 --> 44:26.570
I'd like to take you out to eat.

403
44:32.370 --> 44:35.470
Sure. Dinner tonight, then.

404
44:52.630 --> 44:56.430
So how's the plan to push Din going?

405
44:56.970 --> 44:58.730
It's going great.

406
44:58.730 --> 45:02.030
But lately Din and Star seem to be doing just fine on their own.

407
45:02.400 --> 45:04.330
So I'm just going to sit back and watch.

408
45:05.200 --> 45:07.170
Why are you suddenly rooting for Din?

409
45:07.170 --> 45:09.400
Star liked Physics at first.

410
45:11.070 --> 45:14.070
Sure, my friend liked him, but as his friend,

411
45:14.070 --> 45:16.530
I have to pick what's best for him, right?

412
45:16.530 --> 45:19.500
Din, though? He ticks every box.

413
45:23.000 --> 45:26.430
Oh... What about me?

414
45:28.330 --> 45:29.870
What's my score?

415
45:31.170 --> 45:34.630
What? I already answered that day.

416
45:35.530 --> 45:38.000
Come on, that day was that day.

417
45:38.000 --> 45:42.270
Today, I want to know how much of your heart I've won.

418
46:01.930 --> 46:03.870
Hey, what are you guys doing?

419
46:09.830 --> 46:11.300
Hello.

420
46:12.170 --> 46:15.370
Hey, and you...

421
46:15.370 --> 46:16.530
Oh.

422
46:17.300 --> 46:19.000
I'm shooting content for the council.

423
46:19.830 --> 46:21.230
This song's trending right now.

424
46:22.400 --> 46:24.000
Wait, where's Din?

425
46:24.370 --> 46:25.700
On his way.

426
46:26.000 --> 46:28.100
He's walking Star to the car first.

427
46:28.400 --> 46:30.030
As for today's meeting,

428
46:30.030 --> 46:32.300
keep it short and to the point,

429
46:32.300 --> 46:35.130
because he's got dinner with Star after.

430
46:41.870 --> 46:46.200
"Today's mission" / "Cancel for now" / "Din's killing it!!!"

431
46:47.600 --> 46:48.700
What are you doing?

432
46:49.430 --> 46:51.630
Uh, nothing.

433
46:51.630 --> 46:54.430
Uh, shall we keep practicing the dance?

434
46:54.970 --> 46:56.370
Your turn. Come on.

435
46:58.300 --> 47:00.030
Want to join in?

436
47:14.570 --> 47:16.430
You've come to look at this a few times.

437
47:16.430 --> 47:18.700
Like it? If you do, I'll give you a discount.

438
47:21.630 --> 47:23.370
What's your best price?

439
47:23.370 --> 47:24.470
38,000.

440
47:24.470 --> 47:25.600
That's rock bottom.

441
47:28.470 --> 47:29.700
Can you go any lower?

442
47:29.700 --> 47:32.730
Haggle any more and it's back to 39,000.

443
47:33.230 --> 47:35.330
Then I'll stop haggling.

444
47:54.670 --> 48:00.330
Bro, I think this one's really beautiful.

445
48:04.100 --> 48:06.100
Oh my God.

446
48:17.500 --> 48:23.070
"Chemi, I'm sorry. What do I have to do for you to stop being mad at me?"

447
49:08.170 --> 49:09.500
You possessed or something?

448
49:09.770 --> 49:10.900
No.

449
49:10.900 --> 49:13.370
But I've made up my mind. From now on,

450
49:13.370 --> 49:15.770
I'm going to be a good captain for Thapfah, our school.

451
49:15.770 --> 49:17.800
And a good example for you guys too.

452
49:19.070 --> 49:21.030
What got into you?

453
49:21.930 --> 49:23.570
All right, everyone, listen up.

454
49:24.570 --> 49:27.100
In two weeks, we've got a big tournament.

455
49:27.600 --> 49:31.800
Everyone needs to train harder and take good care of your bodies.

456
49:31.800 --> 49:34.930
Because from now on, training's going to get tougher. Understood?

457
49:34.930 --> 49:36.200
Yes, Coach!

458
49:36.200 --> 49:38.470
Aof, Thanop.

459
49:38.470 --> 49:40.800
You two have to be the backbone of this team.

460
49:43.400 --> 49:44.900
Let's give it everything we've got

461
49:45.400 --> 49:48.170
and bring the championship home to our Thapfah Wittayanusorn School.

462
49:48.170 --> 49:49.570
Let's train hard.

463
49:49.570 --> 49:51.130
Come on! / Let's go!

464
49:53.470 --> 49:58.030
Damn... That's a chemical reaction, all right.

465
50:07.930 --> 50:09.230
Excuse me.

466
50:09.630 --> 50:12.000
Can I practice one more song?

467
50:14.430 --> 50:17.930
I just don't want to be alone.

468
50:18.630 --> 50:21.230
It'll only make me sadder.

469
50:22.600 --> 50:24.000
Oh.

470
50:27.430 --> 50:34.900
Then you pick the next song, Chemi. Two songs, even. Or three.

471
50:35.600 --> 50:38.530
Four songs. We'll stay till morning.

472
50:38.530 --> 50:40.030
Until you're not sad anymore.

473
51:56.730 --> 51:59.970
The student council guys sent these for you.

474
52:01.300 --> 52:02.730
Thank you.

475
52:02.730 --> 52:05.330
But you guys should have the snacks.

476
52:05.900 --> 52:08.800
And there's something special for you too.

477
52:08.800 --> 52:10.600
For me? / Yes.

478
52:10.600 --> 52:14.770
"Warm honey lemon for the singer"

479
52:25.930 --> 52:27.570
Nice work, kid.

480
52:27.570 --> 52:29.570
I don't need compliments.

481
52:29.570 --> 52:31.730
I just want my reward.

482
52:38.270 --> 52:39.870
Thank you.

483
52:56.830 --> 53:01.530
Hmm, it's pricey. Can you handle it?

484
53:01.530 --> 53:03.070
Whatever it costs, I'm in.

485
53:03.070 --> 53:04.830
You sure you can handle it?

486
53:05.100 --> 53:06.700
Absolutely.

487
53:10.630 --> 53:12.570
5,500. / Huh?

488
53:13.030 --> 53:15.070
I thought you said you could handle it.

489
53:18.370 --> 53:20.670
Got the guts or not?

490
53:22.100 --> 53:24.570
Bag this one up for me.

491
53:25.570 --> 53:27.430
You got it, kid.

492
53:30.430 --> 53:32.130
I'll scan to pay.

493
55:03.400 --> 55:05.030
Isn't this a bit much, man?

494
55:06.270 --> 55:07.900
Nah, man.

495
55:08.430 --> 55:10.030
I picked all of it out for you.

496
55:10.030 --> 55:13.270
Once you get all this, you're set.

497
55:14.000 --> 55:15.570
Wait...

498
55:18.900 --> 55:21.230
Start with these basics first.

499
55:22.230 --> 55:24.700
I know you're not great with tenses.

500
55:25.000 --> 55:27.470
Vocab you can memorize later.

501
55:35.430 --> 55:36.800
Ready?

502
55:39.200 --> 55:40.300
Ready, I guess.

503
55:42.300 --> 55:44.330
Hey, come here.

504
55:44.870 --> 55:46.030
What?

505
55:46.570 --> 55:48.000
Turn around, turn around.

506
55:56.030 --> 55:57.230
What's this?

507
55:59.200 --> 56:00.170
Good?

508
56:00.170 --> 56:01.470
Here, let me fix your hair.

509
56:02.070 --> 56:03.100
Ready.

510
56:03.670 --> 56:04.870
Get set.

511
56:10.170 --> 56:11.230
Let's go!

512
56:13.030 --> 56:14.100
Yeah, start from here.

513
56:14.100 --> 56:14.800
Okay.

514
56:16.870 --> 56:20.130
Look, there's Thai here for you to read. Understand it first.

515
56:20.130 --> 56:23.600
Don't rush into the English. That's too advanced.

516
56:24.600 --> 56:30.130
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

517
56:30.130 --> 56:34.330
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

518
56:34.330 --> 56:39.530
♪ a time I've never once forgotten ♪

519
56:42.200 --> 56:50.600
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

520
56:50.600 --> 56:58.000
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

521
56:58.000 --> 57:02.000
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

522
57:02.000 --> 57:06.200
♪ I still remember all our good times, just the same ♪

523
57:06.200 --> 57:10.470
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

524
57:10.500 --> 57:15.200
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

525
57:16.200 --> 57:17.700
What are you doing?

526
57:19.800 --> 57:21.130
Nothing.

527
57:23.330 --> 57:25.170
Why'd you stop reading?

528
57:26.170 --> 57:27.930
Ask first before you do anything.

529
57:27.930 --> 57:29.570
But I'll let that one slide.

530
57:29.570 --> 57:31.170
Let's say I was asleep.

531
57:35.830 --> 57:38.470
You're not focusing.

532
57:49.530 --> 57:51.430
Oh, hello. / Hello.

533
57:52.130 --> 57:54.700
Oh, bye-bye.

534
58:00.000 --> 58:02.400
"I gave it to you, Star. Why'd you give it to your friends?"

535
58:04.070 --> 58:05.500
Bye, Star. Thanks for the snacks.

536
58:05.500 --> 58:07.000
Enjoy.

537
58:07.530 --> 58:08.730
Hey!

538
58:27.070 --> 58:29.170
"Thanks for staying by me. I'm scared as hell."

539
58:29.170 --> 58:31.330
"How'd I cope without you? Thanks, Physics." (Fuen)

540
58:31.330 --> 58:34.330
"I'll try to tell Dad the truth. It must've been hard on you, Aof."

541
58:34.330 --> 58:36.330
"I'm sorry. I'm really, truly sorry." (Memii)

542
58:36.870 --> 58:40.700
"I just wanted to pick you up so we could go to school together." (Din)

543
58:41.400 --> 58:43.470
He's shown me a bunch of universities.

544
58:43.470 --> 58:46.430
So what do you think, Fuen? Study together, or somewhere else?

545
58:46.430 --> 58:48.070
You can stop trying to guess.

546
58:48.070 --> 58:49.430
Is it that obvious on my face?

547
58:49.430 --> 58:52.070
He's studying hard, so no whining, got it?

548
58:52.070 --> 58:53.100
Dad!

549
58:53.100 --> 58:55.770
I've got a big match this Sunday. Will you come watch me, Chemi?

550
58:55.770 --> 58:56.630
I'm busy.

551
58:56.630 --> 58:58.930
But can I have one more chance?

552
59:00.130 --> 59:01.930
Up to you.

553
59:03.030 --> 59:04.030
Thanop.

554
59:04.030 --> 59:05.600
I need five goals on my own today.

555
59:05.600 --> 59:08.130
Dreaming? / I don't have any other choice.

556
59:08.130 --> 59:10.270
Football's the only thing I'm good at.

557
59:10.270 --> 59:12.470
Aof, I can't do that.

558
59:12.470 --> 59:14.100
Or you'll be their target all game.

559
59:14.100 --> 59:15.230
He's rarely this fired up.

560
59:15.230 --> 59:16.600
Coach, why not give him a shot?

561
59:16.600 --> 59:19.330
Three, two, one... Thapfah!
